.SH NAME
.PP
jeopardy.model \(en data types for a Jeopardy game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
from jeopardy.model import Clue, Category, FinalClue, QuestionSet,
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\ \ \ \ Player, Game, Phase
.SH DESCRIPTION
The module defines the data shared by the server, the engine and the
loader.
All types are \f[B]pydantic\f[R](BaseModel) classes, except
\f[B]Phase\f[R].
They hold data only and do no I/O.
.TP
\f[B]Phase\f[R]
A \f[B]str\f[R] enumeration of the stages of a game.
Values: \f[B]lobby\f[R], \f[B]board\f[R], \f[B]wager\f[R],
\f[B]clue\f[R], \f[B]buzz_open\f[R], \f[B]answering\f[R],
\f[B]final_wager\f[R], \f[B]final_answer\f[R], \f[B]final_judge\f[R],
\f[B]game_over\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]Clue\f[R]
\f[B]clue\f[R], \f[B]answer\f[R], \f[B]value\f[R],
\f[B]daily_double\f[R] (default False), \f[B]answered\f[R] (default
False).
.TP
\f[B]Category\f[R]
\f[B]name\f[R] and a list of \f[B]clues\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]FinalClue\f[R]
\f[B]category\f[R], \f[B]clue\f[R], \f[B]answer\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]QuestionSet\f[R]
What is loaded from a file: \f[B]title\f[R] (default \(lqJeopardy\(rq),
a list of \f[B]categories\f[R] and an optional \f[B]final\f[R].
See \f[B]jeopardy\-questions\f[R](5).
.TP
\f[B]Player\f[R]
\f[B]id\f[R], \f[B]name\f[R], \f[B]score\f[R] (default 0),
\f[B]connected\f[R] (default True), and the final round fields
\f[B]final_wager\f[R], \f[B]final_answer\f[R] and
\f[B]final_correct\f[R], all None until set.
.TP
\f[B]Game\f[R]
The complete state of one game: the \f[B]phase\f[R], and the
\f[B]title\f[R], \f[B]categories\f[R] and \f[B]final\f[R] clue copied
from the question set at the start.
\f[B]players\f[R] holds the players by id, the host included, and
\f[B]host\f[R] and \f[B]chooser\f[R] are the ids of the host and of the
player who picks the next clue.
\f[B]current\f[R] is the open clue as (category, index), or None.
\f[B]answerer\f[R], \f[B]tried\f[R] and \f[B]wager\f[R] are who has the
floor, who has already answered the open clue wrongly, and the Daily
Double wager.
\f[B]buzz_opened_at\f[R] and \f[B]lockouts\f[R] time the buzzers, in
seconds on the caller\(cqs clock.
\f[B]log\f[R] holds recent events.
.PP
A \f[B]Game\f[R] can be saved with
\f[B]model_dump\f[R](mode=\(lqjson\(rq) and restored with
\f[B]model_validate\f[R].
The server does this for its state file.
